1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Northern Nigeria. 6:14 AM.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
[Hausa] My name is Aisha. I am the only
health worker in my village.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:30,000
[Hausa] Today I see Fatima. Her ankles are swollen.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Pre-eclampsia kills 50,000 women a year. (WHO, 2023)

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:45,000
[Hausa] There is no signal here. The nearest
doctor is four hours away.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:10,000
[Hausa] Now my phone listens. It sees. It thinks.
All without the internet.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:25,000
[Hausa] It calls the right tools. It writes the
right form. It speaks back — in my language.

8
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:38,000
This is Gemma 4. Open weights. 140 languages.
Audio, vision, and text — in one forward pass.

9
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:55,000
A cloud API can't help Aisha. No signal. Nigerian
law says patient data can't leave the country.
And the API fees would exceed her training budget.

10
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:10,000
When Aisha gets back to town, the visit syncs.
The hospital in Kano knows Fatima is coming.

11
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:25,000
200,000 community health workers in Africa.
1.8 billion people more than two hours from a hospital.

12
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Gemma 4 speaks 140 languages. Hausa today.
Swahili, Quechua, Bambara — next week.

13
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Aisha told us something we won't forget:
"Now, I don't have to guess."

14
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:00,000
CHW Companion — A midwife in every pocket.
Built with Gemma · Apache 2.0
